    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now there was a certain man in Caesarea, Cornelius by name, a centurion of what was called the Italian Regiment,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "At about the ninth hour of the day, he clearly saw in a vision an angel of God coming to him and saying to him, “Cornelius!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "When the angel who spoke to him had departed, Cornelius called two of his household servants and a devout soldier of those who waited on him continually."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now while Peter was very perplexed in himself what the vision which he had seen might mean, behold, the men who were sent by Cornelius, having made inquiry for Simon’s house, stood before the gate,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "Peter went down to the men, and said, “Behold, I am he whom you seek. Why have you come?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "They said, “Cornelius, a centurion, a righteous man and one who fears God, and well spoken of by all the nation of the Jews, was directed by a holy angel to invite you to his house, and to listen to what you say.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "On the next day they entered into Caesarea. Cornelius was waiting for them, having called together his relatives and his near friends."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Peter entered, Cornelius met him, fell down at his feet, and worshiped him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:30",
        "textualBasisJa": "Cornelius said, “Four days ago, I was fasting until this hour; and at the ninth hour, I prayed in my house, and behold, a man stood before me in bright clothing"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 10:31",
        "textualBasisJa": "and said, ‘Cornelius, your prayer is heard, and your gifts to the needy are remembered in the sight of God."
      }
    ],
